Text: We use two public data sets for this purpose: Google Syntactic N-Grams (http://commondatastorage.googleapis.com/books/syntactic -ngrams/index.html) and Probase (Wu et al. Google Syntactic N-grams contains millions of verb phrases, which allows us to mine rich patterns for verbs. Probase contains rich concepts for instances, which enables the conceptualization for objects.

