Text: FrameNet (Baker, Fillmore, and Lowe 1998) is built upon the idea that the meanings of most words can be best under- stood by semantic frames (Fillmore 1976). Semantic frame is a description of a type of event, relation, or entity and the participants in it. And each semantic frame uses frame ele- ments (FEs) to make simple annotations. PropBank (Kings- bury and Palmer 2002) uses manually labeled predicates and arguments of semantic roles, to capture the precise predicate-argument structure.

