=== Generated Answer (model draft; check against evidence) ===
The paper uses two evaluation metrics: coverage and precision [1].

Coverage measures how much of the verb phrases in natural language the solution can find corresponding patterns, and precision measures how much of the phrases and their corresponding patterns are correctly matched [1]. These are computed as coverage = n_cover / n_all and precision = n_correct / n_cover, where n_cover is the number of test-data phrases for which corresponding patterns are found, n_all is the total number of phrases, and n_correct is the number of phrases whose assigned patterns are correct; precision is evaluated by volunteers manually labeling 100 randomly selected verb phrases from the test data [2].
